.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt SYNC 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sync ,
.Nm syncfs
.Nd "write file system updates"
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In unistd.h
.Ft void
.Fn sync void
.Ft int
.Fn syncfs "int fd"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn sync
system call forces a write of dirty (modified) buffers
in the block buffer cache out
to disk.
The kernel keeps this information in core to reduce
the number of disk I/O transfers required by the system.
As information in the cache is lost after a system crash, a
.Fn sync
system call is issued
frequently
by the kernel process
.Xr syncer 4
(about every 30 seconds).
.Pp
The
.Xr fsync 2
system call
may be used to synchronize individual file descriptor
attributes.
.Pp
The
.Fn syncfs
system call writes the dirty data and metadata of the file system
that contains the file referenced by
.Fa fd
to stable storage, and waits for the writes to complete.
The descriptor may reference any file or directory on the file system,
and it may be open for reading only.
Dirty pages of memory-mapped files on the file system are written first.
If the file is on a
.Xr nullfs 4
or
.Xr unionfs 4
mount, the file system that holds the data is written.
On a file system that is mounted read-only,
.Fn syncfs
does nothing and succeeds.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std syncfs
.Sh ERRORS
The
.Fn syncfs
system call fails if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
The
.Fa fd
argument is not a valid descriptor or is an
.Dv O_PATH
descriptor,
or the file system was forcibly unmounted.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The
.Fa fd
argument does not reference a file on a file system,
for example a socket, a pipe or a shared memory object.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
The file system is being unmounted.
.It Bq Er ENOTCAPABLE
The
.Fa fd
argument is a capability without the
.Dv CAP_FSYNC
right.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A signal was delivered while the call waited for a suspended
file system.
.It Bq Er EIO
An I/O error occurred while the file system was written.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fsync 2 ,
.Xr nullfs 4 ,
.Xr syncer 4 ,
.Xr sync 8
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn sync
function conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
The
.Fn syncfs
system call is a
.Fx
extension that is compatible with the Linux system call of the same
name.
Linux also accepts a descriptor that does not reference a file on a
file system.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn sync
function appeared in
.At v3 .
The
.Fn syncfs
system call first appeared in the freebsd-android-native fork of
.Fx 15.1 .
.Sh BUGS
The
.Fn sync
system call
may return before the buffers are completely flushed.
